              2414.0
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Proof. 1.  $ L(U,V) $ is clearly nonempty: the zero mapping O is in it. Theorem 4.2.9 shows that  $ L(U,V) $ is closed under addition and multiplication by scalars. The vector space axioms for  $ L(U,V) $ follow from the corresponding ones in V for every x in y = T(x). In particular, the zero element is the zero mapping O, and the element -T is the mapping  $ (-1)T $.",
          "block_bbox": [
